        "title": "Number Comparison",
        "type": "practiceLevel1",
        "lessons": [
          {
            "title": "Lesson #1",
            "id": 145312,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>We can use comparisons to check things in a game, like whether a player has less health or more score than something else.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #2",
            "id": 145313,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>To check if one value is smaller than another, we use the <strong>less-than operator</strong>, <code>&lt;</code>.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"===\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"25\" endIndex=\"26\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(playerHealth &lt; \" /><text value=\"90\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\");\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>&lt;</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #3",
            "id": 145314,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>If the value on the left is smaller than the value on the right, like in <code>1 &lt; 235</code>, the result is <code>true</code>.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&gt;\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"12\" endIndex=\"13\" /><option startIndex=\"14\" endIndex=\"15\" /><option startIndex=\"16\" endIndex=\"19\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(\" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\" &lt; \" /><text value=\"235\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\");\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>1</code>, followed by <code>&lt;</code>, and finally <code>235</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #4",
            "id": 145315,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>If the value on the left isn't smaller than the value on the right, like in <code>235 &lt; 1</code>, the result is <code>false</code>.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&gt;\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"16\" endIndex=\"17\" /><option startIndex=\"18\" endIndex=\"19\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(\" /><text value=\"235\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\" &lt; \" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\");\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>&lt;</code>, followed by <code>1</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #5",
            "id": 145316,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>To check if one value is bigger than another, we use the <strong>greater-than operator</strong>, <code>&gt;</code>.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&lt;\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"18\" endIndex=\"19\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(score &gt; \" /><text value=\"90\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\");\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>&gt;</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #6",
            "id": 145317,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What do we use the <code>&gt;</code> operator for?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">To check if a score is greater than another score</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">To check if a score is equal to another score</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">To check if a score is greater than another score.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #7",
            "id": 145318,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What do we call the <code>&gt;</code> sign?</p><selection multiple=\"multiple\"><item correct=\"true\" value=\"1\">The greater-than operator</item><item correct=\"false\" value=\"2\">The less-than operator</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">The greater-than operator.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #8",
